On 26 Nov 2017 16:36, <vpbroman@gmail.com> wrote:


One substantive global kind of change was made.
Among all the uses of "la", there were many cases where it is followed by a
verb phrase, and where the expression is not at all a name, but a
description, for example "la tolvirnu cinfo".
All such non-names got "la" replaced with "le".



That looks a deleterious change, unless post-xorlo "le" has been completely
redefined from what it formerly was. The original "la" captures properly
the English, whereas semitraditional "le" does not at all. (By
"semitraditional" I mean to exclude the habitual solecistic misuse that
prevailed in early Lojban writing, where "le" was used as the default
gadri, with sillinesses such as "le nu".)

--And.

